<title>COTE D'IVOIRE: Ivory Coast coffee bean shipments rise in August.</title>
<headline>Ivory Coast coffee bean shipments rise in August.</headline>
<dateline>ABIDJAN 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ivory Coast exported 12,888 tonnes of robusta coffee beans in August against 10,184 tonnes in July, official data show.</p>
<p>Exports in August 1995 amounted to 10,224 tonnes.</p>
<p>Cumulative exports in the first 11 months of the 1995/96 (Oct-Sept) season were 137,150 tonnes against 108,184 in the same period of 1994/95.</p>
<p>The data showed Abidjan, the main port, handled 8,558 tonnes of last month's shipments and 4,330 tonnes left via San Pedro.</p>
<p>A total 651 tonnes of coffee product also left Abidjan but figures were not available for San Pedro.</p>
<p>-- Matthew Bunce, Abidjan Newsroom +225 21 90 90</p>
</text>
